                <pb facs="0171" n="75" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg75"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 3—Translation<anchor n="33"
                            xml:id="d45-f1"/>]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Clarifying Statement to Article 10 Proposed by the
                        Egyptian Government</hi></head>
                <p>“Not wishing either to sell the objects thus found or to form reserves of them
                    for the purpose of rewarding other excavators, the Service des Antiquités is
                    disposed to give the beneficiary of the Permit all objects which it does not
                    require for the national and local collections, whatever may be the importance
                    of the said objects. It is expressly understood that the Service shall have full
                    liberty to form the said collections and that it will decide finally as regards
                    the grant as well as the choice of objects which shall be given to the
                    beneficiary of the Permit.”</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                        1926</hi></date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
